1
00:00:08,904 --> 00:00:11,604
Why, that's a cute little kitten, Ioryogi-san

2
00:00:14,144 --> 00:00:14,444
We can no longer care for her.
Please take her home.

3
00:00:14,444 --> 00:00:16,644
We can no longer care for her.
Please take her home.
We can no longer care for her.

4
00:00:16,644 --> 00:00:17,944
We can no longer care for her.
Please take her home.
Please take her home.

5
00:00:18,384 --> 00:00:21,114
Don't go sticking your nose into
something you can't handle.

6
00:00:21,554 --> 00:00:23,424
She's fluffy!

7
00:00:23,424 --> 00:00:25,324
Were you listening to even a word I said?

8
00:00:25,424 --> 00:00:28,654
I cannot leave the kitten alone.

9
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:30,594
Well then, what do you plan on doing?

10
00:00:32,224 --> 00:00:32,964
Let me care for her.

11
00:00:32,964 --> 00:00:33,764
Let me care for her.
I'm going to do this.

12
00:00:33,764 --> 00:00:34,024
I'm going to do this.

13
00:00:34,094 --> 00:00:39,294
This way the kitten will not be lonely and I
will be able to find someone for her.

14
00:00:40,474 --> 00:00:42,704
Do you plan to live here forever?!

15
00:00:48,644 --> 00:00:51,784
Kobato.

16
00:00:51,784 --> 00:00:54,614
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

17
00:00:54,614 --> 00:00:59,024
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

18
00:00:59,924 --> 00:01:03,224
Muzukashii na

19
00:01:03,224 --> 00:01:05,994
Ureshii toki waratte

20
00:01:05,994 --> 00:01:10,294
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

21
00:01:10,864 --> 00:01:13,304
Na no ni

22
00:01:14,604 --> 00:01:18,974
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

23
00:01:19,404 --> 00:01:22,674
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

24
00:01:22,674 --> 00:01:26,174
Machikirenai yo

25
00:01:26,314 --> 00:01:32,084
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

26
00:01:32,084 --> 00:01:37,294
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

27
00:01:37,294 --> 00:01:40,134
Doko ni aru no?

28
00:01:40,134 --> 00:01:43,464
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

29
00:01:43,464 --> 00:01:46,304
Meippai kizu tsuite

30
00:01:46,304 --> 00:01:49,204
Seiippai hashitte

31
00:01:49,204 --> 00:01:53,174
Nan juu kai koronde naite

32
00:01:53,174 --> 00:01:56,214
Sore de mo mada

33
00:01:56,214 --> 00:02:00,234
Akireru kurai

34
00:02:00,714 --> 00:02:04,884
Ashita wo shinjiteru

35
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:15,334
...A Kitten's Lullaby.

36
00:02:15,334 --> 00:02:18,164
...A Kitten's Lullaby.
You can't even look after yourself.

37
00:02:18,364 --> 00:02:20,634
How do you expect to look after a cat?

38
00:02:21,004 --> 00:02:24,664
But I can't leave her like that.

39
00:02:29,174 --> 00:02:30,974
So now an abandoned cat?

40
00:02:31,384 --> 00:02:35,314
No way. The cat's owner can
no longer care for her.

41
00:02:35,314 --> 00:02:36,414
That's the same.

42
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:41,154
If you don't intend to care for her to
the end, don't get involved.

43
00:02:43,194 --> 00:02:44,884
He's mean.

44
00:02:45,364 --> 00:02:47,264
He's absolutely right.

45
00:02:50,104 --> 00:02:51,724
What's the matter, Kitten?

46
00:02:53,364 --> 00:02:55,094
I-I wonder what's wrong!

47
00:02:55,434 --> 00:02:56,774
She's probably hungry.

48
00:02:56,774 --> 00:02:57,744
Huh?!

49
00:03:01,714 --> 00:03:02,374
Hanamaro Drill
Arithmetic

50
00:03:02,374 --> 00:03:04,344
Hanamaro Drill
Arithmetic
What's the answer to number five, Chiho?

51
00:03:04,344 --> 00:03:05,674
What's the answer to number five, Chiho?

52
00:03:05,784 --> 00:03:08,254
What? You don't know either, Chise?

53
00:03:11,824 --> 00:03:13,084
Yes!

54
00:03:15,094 --> 00:03:15,954
Oh.

55
00:03:15,954 --> 00:03:17,394
It's Kobato.

56
00:03:17,724 --> 00:03:19,024
Hello.

57
00:03:19,724 --> 00:03:21,564
I was hoping you could
satisfy a hungry stomach!

58
00:03:24,904 --> 00:03:26,864
Mother isn't here right now.

59
00:03:27,304 --> 00:03:28,704
This is all we have.

60
00:03:29,374 --> 00:03:32,564
U-Um, I don't think this would work as a meal.

61
00:03:32,774 --> 00:03:33,514
Huh?

62
00:03:33,514 --> 00:03:36,244
Oh, I mean, not for me, but...

63
00:03:36,544 --> 00:03:38,634
It's for this little kitten.

64
00:03:39,244 --> 00:03:40,214
Wow!

65
00:03:40,214 --> 00:03:41,684
So cute!

66
00:03:41,954 --> 00:03:44,854
The owner isn't able to look
after her anymore and...

67
00:03:45,084 --> 00:03:47,924
I was hoping you had
something I could feed her.

68
00:03:47,924 --> 00:03:49,514
Shhh!

69
00:03:50,924 --> 00:03:53,324
Can we come to your room, Kobato?

70
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:55,994
Sure.

71
00:03:59,164 --> 00:04:01,104
She seems to like it.

72
00:04:01,234 --> 00:04:02,634
Good.

73
00:04:02,634 --> 00:04:07,834
Um, why are you two whispering?

74
00:04:09,844 --> 00:04:11,144
Huh? Huh?

75
00:04:13,584 --> 00:04:15,754
Pets are not allowed in this building.

76
00:04:15,754 --> 00:04:21,554
A person living here before had a dog and
neighbors complained about the barking.

77
00:04:21,554 --> 00:04:22,654
So...

78
00:04:22,654 --> 00:04:27,494
Mother decided not to accept
new residents with pets.

79
00:04:28,334 --> 00:04:31,734
Which would mean we can't look after her here.

80
00:04:32,364 --> 00:04:35,394
Why don't you ask the owner again?

81
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:37,304
I don't know who that is.

82
00:04:37,304 --> 00:04:42,474
The kitten was left in a box and the owner's
name wasn't written on it anywhere.

83
00:04:43,274 --> 00:04:48,214
Is that right. But at this rate,
the kitten's going to end up all alone.

84
00:04:48,354 --> 00:04:52,284
If only there's someone who would
agree to take care of her.

85
00:04:55,054 --> 00:04:58,894
I'll ask Ms. Sayaka at the kindergarten tomorrow.

86
00:05:00,594 --> 00:05:03,164
I'm sure that Ms. Sayaka will say yes.

87
00:05:03,164 --> 00:05:06,634
If she's at Yomogi Kindergarten,
we can visit her any time.

88
00:05:06,634 --> 00:05:08,394
Then we'd better name her.

89
00:05:08,674 --> 00:05:10,434
What do you think, Kobato?

90
00:05:10,504 --> 00:05:12,334
What, me?

91
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:14,164
U-Um...

92
00:05:14,444 --> 00:05:17,414
It's too sudden, I can't think!

93
00:05:22,884 --> 00:05:24,884
How about "Milk" 'cause she's pure white.

94
00:05:24,884 --> 00:05:27,114
And she loves milk.

95
00:05:27,454 --> 00:05:32,084
Milk. That's a cute name. It's nice.

96
00:05:33,294 --> 00:05:35,194
Yomogi Kindergarten

97
00:05:35,194 --> 00:05:35,734
Yomogi Kindergarten
Oh so cute!

98
00:05:35,734 --> 00:05:37,004
Oh so cute!

99
00:05:37,004 --> 00:05:38,294
She's pure white!

100
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:40,164
I hear her name's Milk!

101
00:05:41,604 --> 00:05:43,194
Milk, come over here!

102
00:05:43,434 --> 00:05:45,104
Let me hold her!

103
00:05:45,304 --> 00:05:46,344
Me too!

104
00:05:46,344 --> 00:05:47,774
Let me touch her.

105
00:05:48,374 --> 00:05:50,274
Everyone seems happy.

106
00:05:50,514 --> 00:05:52,844
So can you keep her here?

107
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:56,974
Yuzuru.

108
00:05:57,724 --> 00:05:58,914
Come over here for a minute.

109
00:06:02,294 --> 00:06:04,054
Are you all right?

110
00:06:04,294 --> 00:06:07,324
Yuzuru. You might be allergic to cats.

111
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:09,854
Allergic... to cats?

112
00:06:10,334 --> 00:06:12,904
Like with him, allergic people can
start sneezing or get rashes.

113
00:06:12,904 --> 00:06:15,464
If it worsens, it can lead to asthma.

114
00:06:18,774 --> 00:06:20,244
Ms. Sayaka.

115
00:06:20,374 --> 00:06:22,844
We can't keep a cat at the kindergarten.

116
00:06:24,184 --> 00:06:25,614
You're right.

117
00:06:26,514 --> 00:06:28,604
I'm sorry, Kobato.

118
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:33,384
You end up hurting people when you act
without thinking things through.

119
00:06:33,724 --> 00:06:34,824
I wasn't acting without thinking!

120
00:06:34,824 --> 00:06:36,954
Then can you take responsibility?

121
00:06:36,954 --> 00:06:38,444
Fujimoto!

122
00:06:38,694 --> 00:06:40,364
If you're only taking care of it
half-heartedly to satisfy yourself,

123
00:06:40,364 --> 00:06:43,894
you're just as guilty as the
people who abandoned it.

124
00:06:48,474 --> 00:06:50,264
I'm sorry, Kobato.

125
00:06:50,904 --> 00:06:53,204
I'm alright now, though.

126
00:06:53,574 --> 00:06:55,844
No, I'm sorry.

127
00:07:06,184 --> 00:07:07,484
Hey, stop that!

128
00:07:07,654 --> 00:07:11,994
Get away from me! I'm a stuffed
doll but I'm not a stuffed doll!

129
00:07:11,994 --> 00:07:14,124
Kobato, you're here.

130
00:07:15,394 --> 00:07:16,924
Ms. Sayaka.

131
00:07:17,704 --> 00:07:19,394
Can I sit next to you?

132
00:07:19,504 --> 00:07:20,734
Please.

133
00:07:24,374 --> 00:07:26,504
I'm sorry to have disappointed you.

134
00:07:26,504 --> 00:07:29,234
Oh, no. I should be the one apologizing.

135
00:07:30,014 --> 00:07:32,604
Fujimoto doesn't mean ill, you know.

136
00:07:33,284 --> 00:07:38,814
I think he compares himself
to that kitten in some ways.

137
00:07:39,884 --> 00:07:41,154
What?

138
00:07:41,154 --> 00:07:45,714
Oh nothing. I'll help you find
someone to look after the kitten.

139
00:07:46,294 --> 00:07:48,824
Don't worry, we'll find someone, I'm sure.

140
00:07:49,564 --> 00:07:50,534
Yes.

141
00:07:51,834 --> 00:07:54,234
So what do you expect to do now?

142
00:07:54,674 --> 00:07:57,334
I will find someone who can look after Milk.

143
00:07:57,744 --> 00:08:00,144
I cannot cause any more trouble!

144
00:08:00,644 --> 00:08:01,914
I agree.

145
00:08:01,914 --> 00:08:04,034
I've also been troubled enough.

146
00:08:05,884 --> 00:08:07,614
Bye-bye.

147
00:08:09,714 --> 00:08:11,184
Ms. Sayaka.

148
00:08:11,754 --> 00:08:12,884
Hello.

149
00:08:12,884 --> 00:08:14,254
Is Milk here?

150
00:08:19,164 --> 00:08:20,824
Allergic to cats?

151
00:08:20,964 --> 00:08:23,264
I'm afraid so. I'm sorry.

152
00:08:23,534 --> 00:08:24,734
It's all right.

153
00:08:24,734 --> 00:08:26,704
Should we talk to Mother?

154
00:08:26,834 --> 00:08:29,364
No. Pets are not allowed.

155
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:31,764
If we said anything, we'd just make her sad.

156
00:08:32,144 --> 00:08:33,434
You're right.

157
00:08:35,144 --> 00:08:39,084
Can anybody take care of this kitten?!

158
00:08:39,844 --> 00:08:42,574
Please take this kitten home with you!

159
00:08:43,554 --> 00:08:45,524
Look after her, please...

160
00:08:47,054 --> 00:08:48,544
Kobato!

161
00:08:49,694 --> 00:08:51,454
Chiho, Chise.

162
00:08:52,024 --> 00:08:53,464
Hi there, Milk!

163
00:08:53,994 --> 00:08:55,484
Have you been a good girl?

164
00:08:55,634 --> 00:08:59,494
I'm sorry. I asked Ms. Sayaka, but...

165
00:09:00,164 --> 00:09:02,434
We went to the kindergarten.

166
00:09:02,534 --> 00:09:03,564
Huh?

167
00:09:03,734 --> 00:09:05,764
It's not your fault, Kobato.

168
00:09:06,244 --> 00:09:09,934
But I haven't been able to find anyone yet.

169
00:09:10,044 --> 00:09:11,914
We'll help you.

170
00:09:11,914 --> 00:09:15,314
Milk. We'll be sure to find
someone to take care of you.

171
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:21,244
I'm sorry.

172
00:09:21,654 --> 00:09:23,624
My own children are a handful as it is.

173
00:09:26,964 --> 00:09:29,194
Oh my, Katherine, what's the matter dear?

174
00:09:29,534 --> 00:09:30,664
Kobato.

175
00:09:30,664 --> 00:09:31,664
Let's go.

176
00:09:31,664 --> 00:09:33,464
Um, excuse me!

177
00:09:37,274 --> 00:09:39,834
Get out of my face! I hate sales people!

178
00:09:40,374 --> 00:09:41,774
Huh?

179
00:09:42,774 --> 00:09:44,174
Milk!

180
00:09:47,954 --> 00:09:48,284
Hey, what the...

181
00:09:48,284 --> 00:09:49,444
Domoto.
Hey, what the...

182
00:09:50,724 --> 00:09:51,944
Kobato?

183
00:10:08,904 --> 00:10:10,174
Milk!

184
00:10:10,174 --> 00:10:11,464
Come here!

185
00:10:14,444 --> 00:10:16,244
Oh, wow! That's great!

186
00:10:16,844 --> 00:10:19,144
So you need someone to take that kitten.

187
00:10:19,144 --> 00:10:20,384
Yes.

188
00:10:20,384 --> 00:10:25,124
My friends all live alone, so I can't think
of anyone off the top of my head,

189
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:26,414
but I'll see if I can find someone.

190
00:10:26,824 --> 00:10:31,754
Thank you so much. I seem to be causing
everyone a lot of trouble.

191
00:10:32,124 --> 00:10:36,154
I don't think that at all. You're trying so hard.

192
00:10:36,294 --> 00:10:38,464
So we all want to be of help.

193
00:10:38,464 --> 00:10:39,994
No, really...

194
00:10:40,164 --> 00:10:43,764
But you probably should stop
going to strangers' homes.

195
00:10:44,244 --> 00:10:48,614
But Fujimoto told me, " If you're only taking care
of it half-heartedly to satisfy yourself,

196
00:10:48,614 --> 00:10:51,544
you're just like the people who abandoned it".

197
00:10:51,944 --> 00:10:55,784
That's just him. Don't worry about it.

198
00:10:56,414 --> 00:11:01,114
I don't think that anyone would really
want to abandon such a cute kitten.

199
00:11:02,294 --> 00:11:04,854
There must have been a reason.

200
00:11:06,064 --> 00:11:11,054
But when Fujimoto said that,
he looked really lonely.

201
00:11:13,864 --> 00:11:19,674
But he's right. I mustn't tackle this
half-heartedly. I will do everything I can.

202
00:11:20,344 --> 00:11:23,674
Ah, but next time I'll go to homes
where I know the people.

203
00:11:24,214 --> 00:11:27,204
Well then, if you need to reach me,
here's my cell number. Call me.

204
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:31,114
Okay! Thank you very much.

205
00:11:41,964 --> 00:11:44,094
I guess nobody's home.

206
00:11:46,534 --> 00:11:48,294
They're closed.

207
00:12:04,024 --> 00:12:08,724
Hmm... Well you know I handle food.
I can't be having a cat around here.

208
00:12:08,724 --> 00:12:10,584
Is that right.

209
00:12:10,994 --> 00:12:12,924
Sorry I can't help you.

210
00:12:17,764 --> 00:12:20,894
Hello? Mihara residence. Sayaka?

211
00:12:21,504 --> 00:12:23,524
What? A kitten?

212
00:12:24,144 --> 00:12:27,004
I would really like to be able to keep it here but...

213
00:12:29,614 --> 00:12:31,544
The children said that?

214
00:12:32,414 --> 00:12:34,314
Okay. I understand. Thanks.

215
00:12:43,424 --> 00:12:45,224
Oh?

216
00:12:50,164 --> 00:12:52,694
It's getting pretty dark.

217
00:12:53,464 --> 00:12:55,364
Milk's getting tired, too.

218
00:12:57,234 --> 00:12:58,434
Milk?

219
00:12:59,374 --> 00:13:01,774
She must be hungry.

220
00:13:04,984 --> 00:13:06,444
Ready, set...

221
00:13:07,554 --> 00:13:08,714
This one.

222
00:13:10,314 --> 00:13:13,844
I can't do anything. I feel so ridiculous.

223
00:13:14,024 --> 00:13:16,614
Yeah, you can't even buy food for the cat.

224
00:13:16,854 --> 00:13:18,414
No...

225
00:13:24,164 --> 00:13:25,634
Hey Chise.

226
00:13:25,634 --> 00:13:26,834
What is it?

227
00:13:26,834 --> 00:13:29,434
Let's ask Mother anyway.

228
00:13:29,574 --> 00:13:32,304
Yes, I think Mother will understand.

229
00:13:32,304 --> 00:13:34,834
Then we can sleep with Milk tonight.

230
00:13:34,944 --> 00:13:37,034
Mhm. Let's sleep together. You too, Kobato.

231
00:13:37,544 --> 00:13:38,844
Yes.

232
00:13:40,144 --> 00:13:41,544
That lady from...

233
00:13:41,954 --> 00:13:43,214
Oh.

234
00:13:43,414 --> 00:13:45,584
The girl with the pretty singing voice.

235
00:13:45,884 --> 00:13:47,654
Kobato, do you know her?

236
00:13:47,854 --> 00:13:51,024
Yes. Um, where's the baby?

237
00:13:51,524 --> 00:13:55,894
Oh her mother has the day off today,
so she's at home with her.

238
00:13:56,564 --> 00:13:58,264
Oh I see.

239
00:13:59,104 --> 00:14:01,004
But what are you doing here?

240
00:14:01,504 --> 00:14:06,464
I heard there was a girl looking for
someone to take care of a kitten.

241
00:14:06,574 --> 00:14:07,804
What?

242
00:14:08,214 --> 00:14:09,194
Oh my.

243
00:14:10,314 --> 00:14:11,874
This is the kitten, isn't it?

244
00:14:13,184 --> 00:14:15,274
How tiny and cute.

245
00:14:15,814 --> 00:14:19,844
If you don't mind, I'd like to take
her home and care for her.

246
00:14:20,254 --> 00:14:21,724
Really?!

247
00:14:21,724 --> 00:14:26,284
Yes. My grandchild is an only child and I'm sure
she'd be thrilled to have a little playmate.

248
00:14:29,064 --> 00:14:30,624
Oh but...

249
00:14:30,764 --> 00:14:36,504
Some people sneeze or cough when they
touch the kitten. Is the baby okay?

250
00:14:37,234 --> 00:14:40,264
That pizza man was worried
about the same thing.

251
00:14:40,444 --> 00:14:41,604
Pizza man?

252
00:14:41,814 --> 00:14:48,474
Yes. He was asking at every house he delivered
pizzas to, if they could care for a kitten.

253
00:14:48,984 --> 00:14:52,144
I overheard him, and that's what
led me to come here.

254
00:14:54,794 --> 00:14:56,724
That's Fujimoto.

255
00:14:56,954 --> 00:14:59,894
My grandchild loves animals.

256
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:02,584
And she isn't allergic to cats.

257
00:15:02,734 --> 00:15:03,924
Oh, look...

258
00:15:04,734 --> 00:15:06,504
Aren't you lucky, Milk?

259
00:15:06,504 --> 00:15:08,264
You're going to have a nice home.

260
00:15:14,444 --> 00:15:15,674
Good night.

261
00:15:15,674 --> 00:15:17,164
Bye-bye, Milk.

262
00:15:17,274 --> 00:15:19,244
We'll come and visit.

263
00:15:20,514 --> 00:15:21,944
Please wait, ma'am.

264
00:15:23,114 --> 00:15:25,154
This is Milk's food.

265
00:15:25,154 --> 00:15:27,984
My... Yes indeed. Thank you.

266
00:15:30,154 --> 00:15:32,294
Please take good care of Milk.

267
00:15:32,294 --> 00:15:34,314
Y-Yes, please.

268
00:15:45,104 --> 00:15:49,134
This room feels very big without Milk.

269
00:15:49,644 --> 00:15:50,914
Yeah!

270
00:15:50,914 --> 00:15:52,844
Good riddance!

271
00:15:54,514 --> 00:15:55,674
What's this?

272
00:15:56,054 --> 00:15:57,914
Milk's milk dish.

273
00:15:59,454 --> 00:16:03,014
I'm sure that Chiho and Chise
are feeling the same way.

274
00:16:06,824 --> 00:16:08,454
Where are you going?

275
00:16:13,934 --> 00:16:15,074
Kobato.

276
00:16:15,074 --> 00:16:16,694
G-Good evening.

277
00:16:17,304 --> 00:16:18,564
Um...

278
00:16:20,044 --> 00:16:22,014
Chiho and Chise are up on the roof.

279
00:16:28,414 --> 00:16:31,354
I wonder if they're taking good care of Milk.

280
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:34,314
She seemed like a nice grandmother.

281
00:16:35,694 --> 00:16:38,124
Milk is in good hands with that grandmother.

282
00:16:39,124 --> 00:16:40,454
Kobato?

283
00:16:40,864 --> 00:16:42,794
Oh, that...

284
00:16:43,464 --> 00:16:46,054
I forgot to return it to you.

285
00:16:46,704 --> 00:16:47,964
Milk's...

286
00:16:48,404 --> 00:16:49,834
...milk dish.

287
00:16:50,334 --> 00:16:51,604
Yes.

288
00:16:54,204 --> 00:16:59,474
Come to think of it, there was a full moon like
tonight the night I first met that grandmother.

289
00:17:00,084 --> 00:17:03,174
The cherry blossoms were beautiful.

290
00:17:05,324 --> 00:17:10,814
The grandmother was with a baby
who wouldn't stop crying.

291
00:17:11,794 --> 00:17:14,824
I tried to cuddle the baby too.

292
00:17:15,994 --> 00:17:18,764
But then she cried even louder!

293
00:17:18,764 --> 00:17:19,604
And then?

294
00:17:19,604 --> 00:17:20,894
What did you do?

295
00:17:22,604 --> 00:17:26,174
Then I sang her a song.

296
00:17:26,174 --> 00:17:27,344
Huh?

297
00:17:27,344 --> 00:17:29,034
You sang, Kobato?

298
00:17:29,414 --> 00:17:33,174
Yes. And then the baby stopped crying.

299
00:17:33,514 --> 00:17:35,174
What kind of song did you sing?

300
00:17:35,454 --> 00:17:36,474
Huh?

301
00:17:36,654 --> 00:17:38,444
Uh, well...

302
00:17:38,924 --> 00:17:40,024
I'd like to hear it!

303
00:17:40,024 --> 00:17:41,644
Me too!

304
00:17:41,794 --> 00:17:42,894
Huh?

305
00:17:42,894 --> 00:17:44,414
Can you sing it for us, Kobato?

306
00:17:44,624 --> 00:17:45,954
Please.

307
00:17:48,094 --> 00:17:49,534
Okay.

308
00:18:02,474 --> 00:18:08,384
Flowers blossom in the spring

309
00:18:09,084 --> 00:18:14,984
Skies in the summer reach far and wide

310
00:18:15,654 --> 00:18:21,594
Every time I think of this

311
00:18:22,234 --> 00:18:28,234
Precious thoughts spread across in my heart

312
00:18:28,734 --> 00:18:32,474
In the morning when it rains

313
00:18:32,474 --> 00:18:33,774
This song...
In the morning when it rains

314
00:18:33,774 --> 00:18:35,244
In the morning when it rains

315
00:18:35,244 --> 00:18:41,084
On those days when the windows stay closed

316
00:18:41,814 --> 00:18:47,984
My heart shimmers with the light

317
00:18:48,324 --> 00:18:54,594
Light shining brightly above the clouds

318
00:18:55,934 --> 00:19:02,304
The voices are calling to me

319
00:19:02,504 --> 00:19:08,874
From way over yonder, from far I can hear

320
00:19:09,074 --> 00:19:12,884
Voices of laughter

321
00:19:12,884 --> 00:19:15,884
Voices of singing

322
00:19:15,884 --> 00:19:21,884
Echoing voices of the wind

323
00:19:22,154 --> 00:19:28,634
In happiness and in sadness

324
00:19:28,634 --> 00:19:35,204
In all I behold and all that I live for

325
00:19:35,204 --> 00:19:38,974
With my hand in your hand

326
00:19:38,974 --> 00:19:42,014
Your hand in my hand

327
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:48,814
Together, we are one and whole

328
00:20:23,954 --> 00:20:25,074
What is it?

329
00:20:25,324 --> 00:20:28,314
Thank you for your help regarding Milk.

330
00:20:30,994 --> 00:20:33,224
The kitten has found a wonderful home.

331
00:20:33,464 --> 00:20:35,554
Thanks to you, Fujimoto.

332
00:20:37,494 --> 00:20:39,094
Is that all you came for?

333
00:20:39,304 --> 00:20:40,704
Yes.

334
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,264
What are you doing?!

335
00:20:46,674 --> 00:20:49,234
I remembered something very important!

336
00:20:49,614 --> 00:20:51,944
May I borrow your phone?

337
00:20:52,644 --> 00:20:57,844
So if you come across anyone who likes
cats, let me know. Yeah. Thank you.

338
00:21:01,024 --> 00:21:01,554
Kiyokazu Fujimoto

339
00:21:01,554 --> 00:21:02,594
Kiyokazu Fujimoto
Fujimoto?

340
00:21:03,954 --> 00:21:05,054
Hello?

341
00:21:06,594 --> 00:21:09,084
Um... um... well...

342
00:21:09,234 --> 00:21:11,894
Huh? Kobato? What's up?

343
00:21:11,964 --> 00:21:16,804
Yes, uh, um... We found someone
who will take care of the kitten.

344
00:21:17,274 --> 00:21:19,134
I just wanted to let you know.

345
00:21:19,274 --> 00:21:20,244
Oh.

346
00:21:20,244 --> 00:21:23,434
Yes. Fujimoto found someone.

347
00:21:23,744 --> 00:21:24,904
Fujimoto did?

348
00:21:26,884 --> 00:21:28,214
Really.

349
00:21:28,384 --> 00:21:30,944
Sorry to cause all the worry.

350
00:21:31,924 --> 00:21:35,444
No, that's good. See you.

351
00:21:42,164 --> 00:21:43,634
There's more.

352
00:21:43,764 --> 00:21:45,534
But why is there more?

353
00:21:45,534 --> 00:21:49,434
Fujimoto is the one who
found a new home for Milk.

354
00:21:49,674 --> 00:21:51,704
I wasn't any help at all.

355
00:21:51,704 --> 00:21:58,164
Not only that! Because you brought the cat
in here, you caused all sorts of trouble!

356
00:21:59,584 --> 00:22:05,624
Yes. It was all my fault. I caused
everybody a lot of worry and trouble.

357
00:22:05,624 --> 00:22:10,184
Well, you give some you take some.
That's what life's about.

358
00:22:10,324 --> 00:22:11,294
Huh?

359
00:22:11,594 --> 00:22:15,894
You sang for Chiho and Chise because you
realized how lonely they were feeling

360
00:22:15,894 --> 00:22:18,224
after parting with the kitten.

361
00:22:18,564 --> 00:22:22,904
I just wanted to tell them about
that grandmother and the baby.

362
00:22:22,904 --> 00:22:26,344
And I guess you made them
feel better by doing that.

363
00:22:27,504 --> 00:22:31,034
So singing can sometimes be
soothing to the heart too.

364
00:22:31,174 --> 00:22:34,674
But you know... my injured ear has not healed!

365
00:22:35,184 --> 00:22:36,114
Therefore.

366
00:22:36,114 --> 00:22:37,684
Kobato you have zero points!

367
00:22:37,684 --> 00:22:39,444
What?!

368
00:22:40,454 --> 00:22:45,894
Oh, but it's round. Just like today's moon.

369
00:22:45,894 --> 00:22:47,254
This isn't the time to rejoice!

370
00:22:47,924 --> 00:22:51,094
Come to think of it, Milk's dish is round, too.

371
00:22:51,094 --> 00:22:52,664
We're all matching!

372
00:22:52,664 --> 00:22:56,174
All right then, if you like the circle so much,
I'll give you zero every time from now on!

373
00:22:56,174 --> 00:22:59,334
What?! Ioryogi-san, you are so mean!

374
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

375
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

376
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

377
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

378
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Jibun no kage wo

379
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

380
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
Sore nara

381
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

382
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

383
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

384
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

385
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
Shinpai nante iranai yo

386
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Issho ni iru kara

387
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

388
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,094
Fushigi da

389
00:24:26,094 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Memories of Summer.
Fushigi da

390
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,794
Next episode
...Memories of Summer.

